.TH CIGAR 1 "2026-07-12" "CIGAR 0.9.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cigar \- deterministic context, coordination, effect, and replay client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cigar
[global options] command [subcommand] [resource-id]
.SH DESCRIPTION
CIGAR compiles each API-backed command into the frozen operation identifier
and canonical request envelope.
Mutations require explicit confirmation and support dry run.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --output " text|json"
Select human or versioned JSON output.
.TP
.BI --deadline " Nms|Ns|Nm"
Bound the complete operation, up to five minutes.
.TP
.BI --config " path"
Add an explicit CLI configuration layer.
.TP
.BI --target " embedded|local|remote"
Select an explicit execution target.
.TP
.BR --embedded ,
.BR --local ,
or
.BI --remote " URL"
Select a target directly. The remote shortcut requires its HTTPS URL.
.TP
.BI --endpoint " URL"
Override the selected target endpoint.
.TP
.BI --authorization-file " path"
Read bounded authorization material from a protected regular file.
.TP
.BI --input " path"
Read the strict JSON operation request from a bounded regular file.
.TP
.BI --idempotency-key " key"
Reuse one exact mutation reservation.
.TP
.BI --expected-revision " revision"
Bind an optimistic mutation to one exact revision.
.TP
.BI --page-cursor " cursor"
Continue a bounded listing from an opaque cursor.
.TP
.BI --page-size " 1..1000"
Bound one listing page.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Validate and authorize a mutation without committing it.
.TP
.B --yes
Confirm a reviewed state change.
.TP
.B --confirm
Alias of
.BR --yes .
.TP
.B --non-interactive
Disable prompting; unconfirmed mutations fail.
.TP
.B --quiet
Disable progress output.
.TP
.BI --color " auto|always|never"
Control optional terminal color.
.TP
.BI --unicode " auto|always|never"
Control optional Unicode status glyphs.
.TP
.BI --width " 20..1000"
Bound human-readable layout width.
.TP
.B --explain-config
Print effective configuration values and their provenance.
.TP
.B --security
Run the bounded local security checks supported by
.BR doctor .
.TP
.B --deep
Run the complete content-integrity and projection checks supported by
.BR doctor .
.TP
.B --force-full
Ignore an existing signed v5 verified-prefix sidecar and authenticate every
retained checkpoint and delta again. Valid only with
.BR "integrity deep" .
.TP
.BR --help ,
.B -h
Show command help.
.TP
.BR --version ,
.B -V
Show stable build metadata.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Initialize atomic local administration state.
.TP
.B source add|list|refresh|inspect|remove
Manage local CLI source references and run frozen production discovery/status
operations.
.TP
.B ingest
Ingest an accepted discovery plan.
.TP
.B catalog query
Query authorized catalog metadata through the frozen governed retrieval
operation.
.TP
.B status
Report structured target readiness.
.TP
.B context plan|compile|explain|diff|revalidate|materialize
Plan, compile, compare, explain, validate, or materialize context.
.TP
.B project list|attach|detach|switch|link|unlink
Manage project eligibility and explicit disclosure links.
.TP
.B focus new|switch|checkpoint|close
Manage the active context space.
.TP
.B space fork|publish|log|conflicts
Operate and inspect durable context spaces.
.TP
.B handoff create|preview|inspect|accept|revoke|merge
Operate governed handoff capsules.
.TP
.B effect prepare|approve|dispatch|list|inspect|reconcile|compensate
Operate the durable effect journal.
Dispatch and compensation require confirmation.
.TP
.B replay reconstruct|run|compare|completeness
Reconstruct and evaluate replay jobs.
.TP
.B policy check|explain
Evaluate or explain the explicit local production policy profile.
.TP
.B backup create|verify|restore
Create or verify a signed format-two production archive containing the exact
effect checkpoint, or restore it to an explicit empty target only when that
checkpoint still equals current external monotonic truth.
Create and verify take one archive path; restore takes the archive and target
paths.
.TP
.B migration preflight
.I "v4-source.sqlite3 verified-backup new-v5-target.sqlite3"
Re-verify the signed format-two backup and authenticate every retained v4
revision, latest roots, source byte identity, external revision anchor, target
path separation, owner-only modes, and conservative free space. This local
offline preview never creates or mutates the target or source.
.TP
.B migration run
.I "v4-source.sqlite3 verified-backup new-v5-target.sqlite3 --yes"
Repeat preflight under an exclusive runtime lock, construct and deeply verify
the distinct v5 target, retain the unchanged v4 source, and publish a signed
.I .cigar-migration-receipt.json
beside the target. This command does not activate the target.
.TP
.B migration activate
.I "v4-source.sqlite3 verified-backup v5-target.sqlite3 signed-receipt.json active-store.json --yes"
Reacquire exclusive source and target runtime locks; reauthenticate the
retained v4 source, signed backup, signed migration receipt, v5 database,
revision anchor, and complete v5 chain; then atomically publish an owner-only
checksum-protected active-store descriptor. The command fsyncs the descriptor
and parent directory,
reopens the selected v5 target read-only through the published descriptor, and
never deletes the v4 source or backup.
.TP
.B migration cleanup
.I "v4-source.sqlite3 verified-backup incomplete-v5-target.sqlite3 active-store.json --yes"
Explicitly remove only a distinct interrupted target and its closed set of
SQLite, runtime-lock, and revision-anchor sidecars. Cleanup reauthenticates the
retained source and signed backup under exclusive locks, rejects any target
with a signed receipt or active descriptor, and verifies the source remains
byte-identical after target-only deletion.
.TP
.B compaction preview
.I "v5-source.sqlite3 migration-receipt.json new-target.sqlite3 active-store.json new-preview.json --yes"
Create an expiring signed offline preview bound to exact source bytes, active
descriptor generation, migration backup proof, head, policy, pins, candidate
checkpoint/delta range, retained range, and estimated reclaimable bytes.
.TP
.B compaction execute
.I "signed-preview.json --yes"
Reverify every preview binding under the exclusive source lock, copy into the
exact distinct target, remove only the authorized prefix, verify every retained
revision and root, publish a separate signed compaction receipt, and atomically
activate the compacted target. The pre-compaction database remains retained.
.TP
.B compaction status
.I active-store.json
Authenticate and report the current owner-only active descriptor generation,
checksum, and selected database without running maintenance.
.TP
.B integrity deep
.I "v5-database.sqlite3 [--force-full] --yes"
Run SQLite integrity, authenticate every retained checkpoint/delta not already
covered by an unchanged trusted prefix, verify catalog history and the current
projection, and atomically publish a purpose-signed owner-only verified-prefix
sidecar. The prefix is invalidated by database identity, retained origin,
chain, policy, verifier-version, or signature drift. With \fB--force-full\fR
the entire retained range is checked and a corrupt/stale prefix can be replaced.
.TP
.B gc plan|run
Plan or execute bounded, repository-owned encrypted-blob mark-and-sweep.
Plan takes a new signed-plan path and an optional versioned JSON policy
document; run takes that owner-private plan. Physical deletion requires a
current trusted signature, the exact planned repository revision and candidate
set, expired retention and replay windows, no legal hold, a completed backup
policy, and a positive bounded file limit. Before first deletion, run durably
records an owner-private database-and-plan execution marker. An interrupted run
may accept already-absent signed candidates only with that exact marker; newly
visible orphans are retained.
.TP
.BI "diagnostics bundle " archive
Create a deterministic, content-free support archive containing only bounded
build, configuration, platform, inventory, and diagnostic metadata.
.TP
.BI "state inspect-beta " state.json
Strictly inspect an owner-only regular 0.1.0-beta.1 state file. The content-free
plan binds its bytes, generation, and entry counts without emitting identifiers
or paths. It never rewrites the input.
.TP
.BI "state import-beta " "state.json new-backup-directory"
On macOS, verify frozen beta semantics, atomically publish and re-verify
an exact-byte owner-private backup, and then atomically publish the
configured new full-only state directory. Requires confirmation. The
imported schema blocks in-place beta downgrade.
.TP
.B "state restore-beta"
.I "verified-backup-directory new-empty-recovery-directory"
On macOS, re-verify a transition backup and restore its exact beta bytes
into a distinct new empty recovery directory. The configured active full
state is never rewritten.
.TP
.B doctor [--security] [--deep]
Report actionable component diagnostics. Security mode validates protected
local configuration and durable-store settings; deep mode additionally verifies
retained snapshots, journals, blobs, indexes, and exact SQL and full-text
projections without emitting stored content.
.TP
.B serve
Run the installed daemon with the configured production file.
.TP
.B mcp serve
Run the installed stdio MCP adapter.
.TP
.B plugin install|uninstall|doctor claude-code
Preview, install, remove, or diagnose the user-scoped Claude Code adapter
through documented Claude plugin commands. Uninstall preserves portable CIGAR
catalog data.
.TP
.B release verify
Delegate offline release verification to the authoritative installed task.
.TP
.BI "completion " "bash|zsh|fish"
Emit the checked shell-completion asset for the selected shell.
.TP
.B man
Emit this checked manual page.
.TP
.B help
Show the complete command and global-option surface.
.TP
.B version
Show stable build metadata.
.SH SECURITY
Authorization material is read from a bounded regular file and is never emitted.
JSON errors contain only stable public codes, messages, and remediation.
.SH SEE ALSO
cigard(1)
